WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:09.509
When the earthquakes hit, we were out of bed
in quite a hurry.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:15.762
Then we heard the sirens and of course following
the sirens was a voice.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:21.420
And we just, Barbara actually wanted to leave,
she said, "I want to get out of here".

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.930
So we packed up the dogs, got in the car and
took off.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.650
I didn't know there was a siren here in Woodend,
I did not know that and I live here

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.880
and talking to the neighbours, they didn't know either.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.880
We bumped into a lot of people in Rangiora
where we were and talking to them, they were

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:37.940
just confused.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.060
Absolutely.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:42.940
Definitely.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.240
We'd like to know when they are and we'd go
along.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.740
And why did they sound so long after the earthquake?

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.060
That seems weird to me.

